{"study_accession":"PRJNA883612","secondary_study_accession":"SRP400928","title":"Systematic analysis of human antibody response to ebolavirus glycoprotein reveals high prevalence of neutralizing public clonotypes","description":"Understanding the human antibody response to emerging viral pathogens is key to epidemic preparedness. As the size of the B cell response to a pathogenic virus protective antigen is undefined, we performed deep paired heavy and light chain sequencing in EBOV-GP specific memory B cells, allowing analysis of the ebolavirus-specific antibody repertoire both genetically and functionally. This approach facilitated investigation of the molecular and genetic basis for evolution of cross-reactive antibodies by elucidating germline-encoded properties of antibodies to EBOV and identification of the overlap between antibodies in the memory B-cell and serum repertoire. We identified 73 public clonotypes to EBOV, 20% of which encoded antibodies with neutralization activity and capacity to protect mice in vivo. This comprehensive analysis of the public and private antibody repertoire provides insight into the molecular basis of the humoral immune response to EBOV-GP, which informs vaccine design of new vaccines and improved therapeutics.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":8,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN30974388","study_accession":"PRJNA883612","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"run107sample25756","description":"run107sample25756","sex":"male","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-11-02","attributes":[["bio_replicate","107"],["tech_replicate","1"],["seq_type","IgM"],["isolate","Donor 963"],["age","37 years"],["biomaterial_provider","James E Crowe, Vanderbilt Vaccine Center"],["sex","male"],["tissue","PBMC"],["disease","ebola"],["disease_stage","recovered"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR21799333","experiment_accession":"SRX17793314","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selec